## 7. Why We Moved Off Google AI Studio for Animation

AI Studio's Build mode could handle the overall page scaffold and layout fine, but repeatedly failed to translate the "layered dome shapes as hero background art" spec into actual output — it substituted button-internal glow effects and disconnected outline rings instead. Rather than keep iterating blind in Build mode, animation generation moved to Google Flow (Veo) for the wave and hourglass assets, since it produces an actual renderable clip you can inspect directly rather than a text-described implementation that may or may not match intent. Trade-off: Flow output is fixed video, not an editable vector/Lottie file — no built-in frame markers or code-level scrubbing. The hourglass piece still works fine with this constraint via manual `video.currentTime` scrubbing; the wave assets simply become background/overlay video instead of a re-colorable vector loop.

